+# Motion budgets in Otomat
+
+This local policy resolves the vendored duration and property recommendations.
+Keep the purpose/frequency gate and reduced-motion support in every workflow.
+
+UI motion defaults to under 300 ms. Press feedback uses 100–160 ms, tooltips
+125–200 ms and dropdowns 150–250 ms. The 200–500 ms modal/drawer range is an
+exception for occasional spatial transitions: justify the travel or gesture,
+measure responsiveness, and keep controls usable during motion. A 400 ms toast
+example illustrates that exception, not the default for every toast. Marketing
+or explanatory motion may be longer when it does not delay interaction.
+
+Prefer transform and opacity. A height transition is an exception when expansion
+must move surrounding content and a transform cannot express it. Verify its
+layout cost, interruption behavior and reduced-motion alternative. Do not add
+layout animation to a busy list for decoration. Reviewers apply these same
+exceptions; an example alone does not justify one.
